## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates understanding of multi-tenant isolation in cloud-native ML serving, per-tenant observability, and governance in AWS SageMaker.

## Key Concepts
- Multi-tenant routing with PrivateLink for network isolation
- Per-tenant Feature Store namespaces for data isolation
- Canary deployments with automated rollback on drift or latency degradation
- Per-tenant monitoring, autoscaling, and governance via Model Registry

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code: Route inference request to tenant-specific endpoint
function routeToTenant(req, tenantId) {
  const endpoint = tenantEndpoints.get(tenantId);
  if (!endpoint) throw new Error('Unknown tenant');

  const result = await invokeEndpoint(endpoint, req.payload);

  // Check latency and trigger rollback if needed
  if (result.latencyP99 > latencyThreshold) {
    triggerAutoRollback(tenantId);
    alertOnCallers(tenantId, 'Latency spike detected');
  }

  return result;
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
This evaluates expertise in deploying real-time ML systems within AWS for privacy-sensitive, multi-tenant environments requiring comprehensive monitoring, explainability, and rapid recovery capabilities.

## Key Concepts
- AWS PrivateLink and SageMaker endpoint architecture
- Private data lake integration with strict multi-tenant isolation
- Real-time drift detection and SHAP/IG explainability frameworks
- Provisioned concurrency and autoscaling for performance targets

## Code Example
```javascript
// Explainer integration for inference transparency
function explainInference(model, input, featureNames) {
  const shapValues = model.predictSHAP(input);
  const igValues = model.predictIntegratedGradients(input);
  return {
    prediction: model.predict(input),
    explanations: {
      shap: shapValues,
      integratedGradients: igValues,
      featureNames: featureNames
    },
    timestamp: new Date().toISOString(),
    tenantId: extractTenantId(input)
  };
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Assesses design for multi-tenant ML services with strict data residency, private networking, and production-grade reliability, including canarying, drift handling, and cost accounting.

## Key Concepts

- PrivateLink and VPC isolation
- Multi-tenant routing architectures (per-tenant vs shared endpoint)
- Canary deployments with automatic rollback on drift/latency
- SageMaker Model Monitor for drift and quality checks
- KMS encryption and data residency controls

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-routing logic (illustrative only)
function routeRequest(tenantId, payload) {
  const endpoint = selectEndpointForTenant(tenantId);
  return invokeSageMaker(endpoint, payload);
}

function selectEndpointForTenant(tenantId) {
  // tenants mapped to endpoints or routing keys
  const map = {
    't1': 'endpoint-arn-1',
    't2': 'endpoint-arn-2'
  };
  return map[tenantId] || 'shared-endpoint-arn';
}
```

